WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.520
if you are planning a ribbed band that's

2
00:00:03.720 --> 00:00:08.720
going to be doubled, maybe for a neck
band, here's a tip to try.

3
00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:12.760
Add a turning row for a more defined edge.

4
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:20.360
When you reach the halfway point of your
band, knit two rows on the main bed only

5
00:00:21.120 --> 00:00:24.520
and slip the ribber stitches.

6
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.640
Then finish knitting the band.

7
00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:33.520


8
00:00:34.600 --> 00:00:37.560
In this example, you can see that this

9
00:00:37.760 --> 00:00:43.200
creates a crease. But you can
also see the slipped strands.

10
00:00:45.640 --> 00:00:48.600
In this 1x1 example,

11
00:00:48.690 --> 00:00:54.200
we also get the crease.
and
the slipped strands aren't as noticeable.

12
00:00:54.400 --> 00:00:58.520
In this example, I only slipped one row.

13
00:00:58.720 --> 00:01:01.200
The crease isn't as defined.

14
00:01:01.400 --> 00:01:06.880
This technique is an improvement over
just folding the ribbing in half.

15
00:01:07.080 --> 00:01:11.240
But please take a time to give this
a try before using it on a project.

16
00:01:11.440 --> 00:01:12.920
and
let me know what you think.

